WEBVTT

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:34.734
Over the past 200 years, economies have
gotten exponentially more efficient

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.194
at producing value.

00:02:36.694 --> 00:02:40.740
If we, as a species, 
are able to keep upgrading our economies

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.284
so that they get ever-more efficient,

00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:48.289
we could theoretically pump out 
more and more value using the same—

00:02:48.289 --> 00:02:52.084
or, let’s be really ambitious here— 
fewer resources.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.086
So, how do we do that?

00:02:54.086 --> 00:02:56.589
How do we increase efficiency?

00:02:56.964 --> 00:02:58.758
With new technologies.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.968
This is where we hit a snag.